CHMOD(1)                       User Commands                        CHMOD(1)

NAME
    chmod - change a file's permission bits

SYNOPSIS
    chmod MODE PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Set the permission bits of PATH to MODE, which is octal, one to four
    digits (for example 644 or 0755). There is no symbolic form, and a
    mode that does not parse is refused rather than partly applied.

SECURITY
    The owner of a file may change its mode, and so may the administrator.
    The fs_server decides, against the identity the kernel attests for
    your login, never against anything the shell says.

SEE ALSO
    stat(1), chown(8)
